NEW = [
    ("p:who-takes-part", "The rules bar participation fees and exclude no registered expert, yet only those who bear the cost of taking part, or whose sponsors do, get a vote. They propose for needs they and their sponsors know, and since users differ from participants in which features matter, the needs reaching a vote need not match users' needs.", "same clauses, regrouped"),
    ("p:merit-gap", "Winning a consensus call and producing the design that serves users best coincide only as far as voters can judge that at the poll and weigh it above other values. SD-4 assigns no one to judge it for them.", "'their other values' is 'other values'"),
    ("p:integration", "No step in SD-4 checks whether separately adopted designs work together, and each author gains from their own design's adoption while a conflict costs users and later rework. The nearest steps ask a good paper to fit the language's principles, have new wording written against the adopted drafts, and let a TS merge early for integration testing.", "'costs users and whoever must later rework them' is 'costs users and later rework'"),
    ("l:author-knows-more", "SD-4 relies on the presenter, an expert in the paper's domain, to educate a room of general C++ experts. It also counts a feature's designers among the best experts on any concern about it.", "split in two"),
    ("p:disclosure", "Stating a drawback in the paper before an early poll can cost Favor votes when incumbency is decided, while a better-informed vote's gain is spread across the design's users. SD-4 says a good paper should show the alternatives considered, but it asks no paper to state its design's drawbacks, and a paper is considered without them.", "'cost the author Favor votes' is 'cost Favor votes'"),
    ("p:written-answer", "No rule requires a written answer to an objection, apart from an author's defense of declining a directed change and ISO's response to each enquiry ballot comment. For the author, a written answer makes the objection easier to raise again, but also shows later what would not be new, the test SD-4 applies to repeated objections.", "'SD-4 sorts repeated objections by new information' is 'the test SD-4 applies to repeated objections'"),
    ("p:miss-cost", "A proposal that misses an edition's feature cutoff waits at least for the next edition, planned three years later. It can ship sooner as a white paper, which has no prescribed schedule, and the same schedule keeps an unfinished feature from delaying the features that are ready.", "'unless it ships sooner' is 'It can ship sooner'"),
    ("p:cutoff-effect", "At the feature cutoff, a one-meeting delay for a paperless rival, or an Against vote keeping a proposal below the 2:1 line, sends it to the next planned edition.", ""),
    ("p:prefer-is", "A TS delays IS adoption by about one to two years, and its experience can bring incompatible changes first: a gain to result-seeking authors, a risk to design-bound ones. The design room can still require a TS, and ISO and SC22 now recommend the lighter white paper.", "'breaking changes' is 'incompatible changes'"),
    ("p:nb-comment", "A national body's No opposes every feature in the document at once, including ones its own experts support, while WG21 considers its comments whatever its vote. A body valuing the rest of a document above blocking one feature does better voting Yes with comments, and one wanting the work in no form does better voting No.", ""),
    ("l:rank-rest-yes", "A body that values the rest of a document above blocking any one feature ranks Yes with comments above abstaining. That holds because only the Yes counts toward the approval it prefers, and its comments are considered either way.", "split in two; 'since' becomes 'That holds because'"),
    ("p:nb-members", "A national body forms its position by its panel's own rules, which SD-4 does not state, so whether a sponsor's paid participants add weight there depends on those rules. In the United States, INCITS gives a voting member's representatives one vote, apart from up to four Defense Department votes, and bars consultants a voting member funds from voting membership.", "'share its single vote' is 'one vote'"),
]
